Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 08:26:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] =?UTF-8?q?DSpark=20port:=20row=20commit=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20per-row=20frontier=20capture=20kills=20partial-accept=20repl?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ay?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The batch verifier now optionally captures the small per-layer compressor
frontier state (plus append counters) after every speculative row, priced at
~0.4 ms per row of device-side copies. A partial accept of any prefix length
commits by copying one captured row back instead of restoring the pre-verify
snapshot and replaying the accepted tokens through a second full verifier
pass, which cost 120-175 ms per partial accept on GB10 and made stock
--mtp-draft > 2 a net loss. Enabled with --dspark-row-commit.

Speculative captures also force the per-token compressor path in the batch
encoder: the aligned-chunk compressor computes only the final frontier, so
mid-chunk state does not exist there. This also closes a latent hole where
the stock prefix1 capture never fired for ratio-2 layers at even start
positions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
